 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "At the hotel",
     "texto": [
      "On arrival: **よやく が あります** (I have a booking).",
      "Rooms: **シングル** (single), **ツイン** (twin, with two beds). Nights are counted with **はく**: **いっぱく** (one night), **にはく** (two nights).",
      "In hotels they will speak to you very respectfully: they add **さま** instead of **さん** to your name, and they say **おへや** instead of **へや**.",
      "Floors are counted with **かい** (sometimes «がい»): **3 がい** (third floor).",
      "To confirm: **はい、 そう です** (yes, that's right)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "If you don't feel well",
     "texto": [
      "**だいじょうぶ です か** = are you all right? And the answer: **だいじょうぶ です** (I'm fine).",
      "Pains are said with the part of the body + **が いたい です**: **あたま が いたい です** (my head hurts), **おなか が いたい です** (my tummy hurts).",
      "**ねつ が あります** = I have a fever.",
      "In Japanese, medicine is «drunk»: **くすり を のみます**.",
      "To someone who is ill you say **おだいじに** (get well soon)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
